    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "comment-1",
        "text": "MAPS\n\nA map (HashMap) stores values by KEY: here an inventory from item name to quantity (as text).\nMap nodes return a NEW map, so each Insert feeds the next one along a wire. Length, Contains Key,\nKeys and To JSON then answer questions about the finished map.\nClass variables hold single values (numbers, text, booleans), so the collection itself lives on the wires between nodes and only the answers are stored in variables.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          -300.0
        ],
        "size": [
          900.0,
          210.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.4,
          0.8,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-2",
        "text": "FILL THE MAP\nHashmap New, then three Inserts (key and value typed on each node): sword=1, shield=2, potion=5. Each Insert passes the bigger map to the next.",
        "position": [
          60.0,
          720.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1260.0,
          100.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.3
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "new",
          "ins0",
          "ins1",
          "ins2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "comment-3",
        "text": "QUESTIONS\nLength = 3, Contains Key \"sword\" = true, To JSON = the whole map as text. Keys returns an array (in no guaranteed order) which String Join turns into a comma-separated list.",
